Platform standardization establishes common technical standards across Azure environments.

Areas commonly standardized include:

* Virtual machine images
* Network architecture
* Identity management
* Monitoring
* Logging
* Backup policies
* Naming conventions
* Resource tagging

# Real-Life Example:
For example, every production workload may use identical monitoring agents and backup schedules regardless of business unit.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is multinational organizations simplifying operations across hundreds of Azure subscriptions.

Platform standardization improves efficiency and simplifies support.
